{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I send an angel.</b> Here they were foretold that they were destined to sin, and the Shechinah says to them: ״כִּי לֹא אֶעֱלֶה בְּקִרְבְּךָ״ (Exodus 33)." "<b>Which I have prepared.</b> Which I designated to give you — this is its plain sense; and its midrash — <b>to the place which I have prepared</b>: already My place corresponding to it. And this is one of the verses that say that the heavenly Temple is set corresponding to the earthly one (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:10.690906968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}